WEBVTT

NOTE
The 40-second tour of Board. The film has music and sound effects and no speech;
these captions describe what's on screen.

00:00.000 --> 00:03.600
[Soft music] Board's icon and name.
“Your work, on paper.”

00:03.700 --> 00:07.400
“Plan the week.”
Four columns, one glance. Drag a card and it just moves.

00:07.400 --> 00:11.300
⌘N adds a card to To do, and “Review pricing page with design” is dragged into In progress. [Soft thock]

00:11.300 --> 00:12.600
“Priorities, groups, notes and comments, one click away.”
The task's details slide in.

00:12.700 --> 00:16.600
“Every week, a fresh page.”
Tasks live in their week. Travel back, look ahead, carry what's left.

00:16.600 --> 00:19.600
⌃⌘← and ⌃⌘→ travel between weeks, and the unfinished tasks are carried into the new one. [Chime]

00:19.700 --> 00:23.300
“Everything else, at a glance.”
Meetings, prayer times, mail, and the work waiting for you elsewhere.

00:23.300 --> 00:26.600
The meeting countdown ticks to 23 minutes. GitHub's review requests open.
Everything is read-only, and tokens stay in your Mac's Keychain.

00:26.700 --> 00:30.600
“Step away, and it breathes.”
Ambient mode: living scenes, a clock and your glances.

00:30.600 --> 00:34.600
A caravan crosses the desert at dusk, then the water rises into the ocean and a whale swims by. [Wind, then underwater sounds]

00:34.700 --> 00:39.300
Board: a calm place for your work. For macOS.
Read-only integrations · Keychain-safe · Keyboard-first
